// ================================================================================================
// V60 -- DONCHIAN BREAKOUT + EMA CROSS CONFIRMATION + AROON OSCILLATOR + CHOP/ADX REGIME
//
// Two presets, every component switchable, and each switch states its own MEASURED cost. The
// research is `docs/ib/STUDY_V60_AROON.md`: 1,166,400 configurations evaluated on 60-minute bars
// across US100 (51,889 bars), NQ (18,243) and US30 (49,325), of which 142,560 per market are
// DISTINCT once the inert axes are collapsed.
//
// ============================ READ THIS BEFORE TURNING THE AROON ON ============================
// THE AROON OSCILLATOR CANNOT FILTER THIS STRATEGY, AND IT IS AN IDENTITY RATHER THAN A WEAK
// SIGNAL. Aroon Up(N) is 100 exactly when the newest bar of its window is the window's highest. A
// Donchian(E) long breakout fires when the close exceeds the prior E-bar high. So WHENEVER
// N <= E THE BREAKOUT BAR IS THE N-BAR HIGH BY CONSTRUCTION: Aroon Up is 100 and the oscillator
// is non-negative, always. Checked bar by bar on all three markets:
//
//   market   donchian  aroon N   breakout bars   Aroon Up == 100   osc >= 0   osc >= 50
//   US100        20       14         4,114           100.0%          100.0%      74.8%
//   US100        30       25         3,407           100.0%          100.0%      84.0%
//   NQ           20       14         1,370           100.0%          100.0%      72.0%
//   NQ           55       25           875           100.0%          100.0%      80.5%
//   US30         30       25         2,878           100.0%          100.0%      86.2%
//   US30         55       25         2,291           100.0%          100.0%      88.3%
//
// ZERO EXCEPTIONS in every cell where N <= E. `osc >= 0` and `up >= 70` cannot remove ONE signal.
// The proof is visible in the P&L: at Donchian 55 with Aroon 25 the three readings below are the
// SAME NUMBERS TO THE CENT as Aroon off --
//
//   aroon at don 55/20 + CHOP<=45      US100 res/lock        NQ res/lock        US30 res/lock
//   off                              +48.70 / +84.83     +130.03 / -44.65    +232.91 / +92.12
//   osc >= 0   (25)                  +48.70 / +84.83     +130.03 / -44.65    +232.91 / +92.12
//   up  >= 70  (25)                  +48.70 / +84.83     +130.03 / -44.65    +232.91 / +92.12
//   osc >= 50  (25)                  +57.94 / +37.69     +135.91 / -148.77   +213.91 / +101.52
//
// Only `osc >= 50` binds at all, and it is the one that damages the locked block. The HUD on this
// script prints the live pass rate of your Aroon setting ON BREAKOUT BARS so you can watch the
// identity hold on your own chart: if it reads 100.0%, the filter is doing nothing.
//
// Over the WHOLE grid, no Aroon setting beats `off` in more than 2 of the 6 market-block columns,
// and the differences are +-1 dollar a trade on a base of 25 to 90. Aroon also correlates
// +0.57 to +0.60 with the EMA state it is being added to, so it is not even an independent second
// reading. IT SHIPS OFF. It is wired, plotted and counted rather than deleted, so the claim can be
// re-checked rather than taken on trust.
//
// ================================ WHAT THE GRID SAYS DOES HELP ================================
// Marginal average per axis over the whole grid (never the top row -- that is the maximum of
// 132,396 draws). A setting earns its place only by beating `off` in ALL SIX market-block columns.
//
//   EMA condition on (either form)      5 of 6   the only trigger component that carries
//   NO TAKE PROFIT                      5 of 6   fifth independent confirmation on this branch
//   wide stop (3.0 x ATR)               4 of 6   the stop axis is monotone toward wider
//   long entry channel (55)             5 of 6
//   long exit channel (20)              5 of 6
//   CHOP(14) <= 45                      4 of 6
//   ADX(14) >= 20                       2 of 6   the WEAKER gate, and the top cell uses it
//   AROON, every setting             <= 2 of 6   see above
//
// ================================== THE TWO PRESETS =====================================
// PRESET A -- RESEARCH TOP CELL. EMA 21/62 cross, confirm within 40 bars, Donchian 10 entry /
// 10 exit, 3.0N stop, no target, ADX >= 20. This is the configuration that was actually put
// through the gates: it clears a minute-of-day matched control on US100 (p 0.000) and US30
// (p 0.005) and fails on NQ (p 0.062); day-block bootstrap P(mean<=0) 0.000 / 0.017 / 0.001 on
// research. Read once on locked: PF 1.250 / 1.056 / 1.127 against research 2.143 / 1.831 / 1.893.
//
// PRESET B -- MARGINAL CONSENSUS. The same rule at the settings the WHOLE grid prefers rather
// than the settings its top row happens to carry: Donchian 55 entry / 20 exit, CHOP <= 45 instead
// of ADX. Its locked numbers are better on two of three markets. THAT COMPARISON IS A LOCKED-BLOCK
// READ AND IS NOT A SELECTION: preset A is what was chosen on research and validated, and B is
// offered because the marginal table -- computed on research alone for don_e and don_x -- prefers
// those settings. Treat B as a hypothesis, not as an improvement.
//
// =============================== WHAT THIS SCRIPT DOES NOT CLAIM ===============================
// * NOTHING HERE SHIPS AS AN EDGE. The one-rung neighbourhood of preset A is 128 of 128 cells
//   profitable on research on all three markets and 26.6% profitable on NQ's locked block. That is
//   a perfect plateau that does not replicate. corr(research, locked) across 121,282 NQ
//   configurations is -0.4426.
// * THE CHANNEL EXIT FILLS AT THE NEXT BAR'S OPEN HERE and at the breaking bar's CLOSE in the
//   research engine, because a script cannot place a market-on-close order decided by the close it
//   fills at. An independent vectorbt build measured that convention at 1.9 to 10.3 points a trade
//   and up to 353 points on a single trade across an overnight gap, and under it the locked block
//   reads +5.98 / -12.28 / -0.09 against the engine's +17.36 / +6.81 / +14.94. EXPECT THIS SCRIPT
//   TO UNDERPERFORM THE RESEARCH NUMBERS, and that direction is the honest one.
// * The costs below are MNQ's ($1.44 round turn, one tick of slippage). CHANGE THEM for any other
//   instrument -- a cost is a fraction of the risk being taken, not a number of points, and
//   charging one instrument's fees on another has produced a decisive-looking failure here before.
//   Read the TRADE COUNT and the COMMISSION LOAD before the P&L.
// * Long only. The short mirror of this family loses on every block measured on this branch.
// * All hours, no flatten. A fixed-time flatten is destructive on every window tested here -- nine
//   independent confirmations -- because it truncates exactly the trades a channel exit exists to
//   hold.
//
// Research tooling for education and analysis. Not financial advice.
// ================================================================================================
//@version=6
strategy("V60 Donchian + EMA cross + Aroon", overlay = true, pyramiding = 0,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     initial_capital = 50000, currency = currency.USD,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_order, commission_value = 0.72,
     slippage = 1, calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = false)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUTS
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gP = "Preset"
preset = input.string("A - research top cell", "Preset", group = gP,
     options = ["A - research top cell", "B - marginal consensus", "Custom"],
     tooltip = "A is the configuration that went through the matched control, the Monte Carlo and " +
     "the robustness box. B is what the whole grid's marginal average prefers. Custom uses every " +
     "input below exactly as set.")

gE = "Entry -- EMA confirmation"
emaModeIn = input.string("cross", "EMA condition", group = gE,
     options = ["off", "state", "cross"],
     tooltip = "off: the Donchian breakout alone. state: fast above slow. cross: a breakout " +
     "within N bars AFTER an upward cross. Marginal: the EMA condition on beats off in 5 of 6 " +
     "market-block columns -- the only trigger component that does.")
emaFastIn = input.int(21, "EMA fast", minval = 2, group = gE)
emaSlowIn = input.int(62, "EMA slow", minval = 3, group = gE)
confirmWinIn = input.int(40, "Confirmation window (bars after the cross)", minval = 0, group = gE,
     tooltip = "Only used in `cross` mode. 0 means no recency requirement at all, which is the " +
     "grid's own Donchian-alone ablation.")

gD = "Entry -- Donchian and exits"
donEntryIn = input.int(10, "Donchian entry length", minval = 2, group = gD,
     tooltip = "A is 10 (the top cell). The grid's marginal average prefers 55, in 5 of 6 columns.")
donExitIn = input.int(10, "Donchian exit channel length", minval = 2, group = gD,
     tooltip = "A is 10. The marginal average prefers 20, in 5 of 6 columns.")
stopNIn = input.float(3.0, "Stop, x ATR(20 Wilder)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = gD,
     tooltip = "The stop axis is monotone toward WIDER across the whole grid. 3.0 is the grid edge.")
tpRIn = input.float(0.0, "Take profit, R (0 = none)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.5, group = gD,
     tooltip = "0 is best in 5 of 6 columns. No take profit has now beaten every target tested " +
     "five separate times on this branch. Setting this above zero is going against that.")

gR = "Regime gate"
useAdxIn = input.bool(true, "ADX(14) floor", group = gR,
     tooltip = "Beats `off` in only 2 of 6 market-block columns. It is in preset A because the " +
     "top cell carries it, not because the marginal table supports it.")
adxMinIn = input.float(20.0, "ADX minimum", minval = 0.0, step = 1.0, group = gR)
useChopIn = input.bool(false, "CHOP(14) ceiling", group = gR,
     tooltip = "Beats `off` in 4 of 6 columns -- the better-supported of the two gates, and the " +
     "one preset B uses.")
chopMaxIn = input.float(45.0, "CHOP maximum", minval = 0.0, step = 1.0, group = gR)

gA = "Aroon oscillator"
aroonModeIn = input.string("off", "Aroon condition", group = gA,
     options = ["off", "osc >= 0", "osc >= 50", "osc >= -50", "up >= 70"],
     tooltip = "SHIPS OFF, and the reason is arithmetic rather than a weak result. Whenever the " +
     "Aroon length is <= the Donchian entry length, `osc >= 0` and `up >= 70` are TRUE ON EVERY " +
     "BREAKOUT BAR by construction and remove nothing. Watch the HUD's `pass on breakouts` row.")
aroonLenIn = input.int(25, "Aroon length", minval = 2, group = gA)
showAroonIn = input.bool(true, "Report the oscillator in the status line / data window", group = gA,
     tooltip = "This script is an overlay, so the oscillator is NOT drawn on the price scale -- " +
     "it would squash the chart. Its live value appears in the status line, the Data Window and " +
     "the panel instead.")

gH = "Display"
showHudIn = input.bool(true, "Show the diagnostic panel", group = gH)
showLevelsIn = input.bool(true, "Plot the Donchian channels", group = gH)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PRESET RESOLUTION. Done here in main scope, once, so every downstream line reads one variable.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
isA = preset == "A - research top cell"
isB = preset == "B - marginal consensus"

emaMode = isA or isB ? "cross" : emaModeIn
emaFast = isA or isB ? 21 : emaFastIn
emaSlow = isA or isB ? 62 : emaSlowIn
confirmWin = isA or isB ? 40 : confirmWinIn
donEntry = isA ? 10 : isB ? 55 : donEntryIn
donExit = isA ? 10 : isB ? 20 : donExitIn
stopN = isA or isB ? 3.0 : stopNIn
tpR = isA or isB ? 0.0 : tpRIn
useAdx = isA ? true : isB ? false : useAdxIn
adxMin = isA or isB ? 20.0 : adxMinIn
useChop = isA ? false : isB ? true : useChopIn
chopMax = isA or isB ? 45.0 : chopMaxIn
aroonMode = isA or isB ? "off" : aroonModeIn
aroonLen = isA or isB ? 25 : aroonLenIn

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SERIES. ATR is ta.atr, which is Wilder's rma(TR, n) -- and that is deliberate here: the research
// used rma(TR, 20), not this branch's usual ema(TR, n), because the family started from a Turtle
// definition. Do not "fix" it to ta.ema(ta.tr(true), n).
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
atrVal = ta.atr(20)

emaF = ta.ema(close, emaFast)
emaS = ta.ema(close, emaSlow)
emaUp = emaF > emaS
emaCross = ta.crossover(emaF, emaS)

// GUARDED. `ta.crossover` reads `close`, which differs mid-bar, and `lastCrossBar` is DURABLE
// state that decides which breakouts are eligible. An unguarded write here is exactly the Turtle
// script's `lastWin := close > firstFill` defect: a cross that happens intrabar and unwinds by the
// close would still arm the confirmation window forever.
var int lastCrossBar = na
if emaCross and barstate.isconfirmed
    lastCrossBar := bar_index
barsSinceCross = na(lastCrossBar) ? -1 : bar_index - lastCrossBar

emaOk = emaMode == "off" ? true : emaMode == "state" ? emaUp :
     confirmWin <= 0 ? barsSinceCross >= 0 :
     barsSinceCross >= 0 and barsSinceCross <= confirmWin

// ta.dmi returns [+DI, -DI, ADX] IN THAT ORDER. Destructuring only the first element substitutes
// +DI for ADX silently, which has shipped broken on this branch once.
[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(14, 14)

chopLen = 14
chopRange = ta.highest(high, chopLen) - ta.lowest(low, chopLen)
chopVal = 100.0 * math.log10(math.sum(ta.tr(true), chopLen) / math.max(chopRange, syminfo.mintick)) /
     math.log10(chopLen)

// AROON, written to match the research construction EXACTLY: its window is the last N+1 bars
// (i-N .. i) and Up is 100 * (offset of the highest from the oldest) / N, so the current bar being
// the highest gives 100 and the oldest bar being the highest gives 0. ta.highestbars returns a
// non-positive offset from the current bar, hence the + aroonLen.
aroonUp = 100.0 * (ta.highestbars(high, aroonLen + 1) + aroonLen) / aroonLen
aroonDn = 100.0 * (ta.lowestbars(low, aroonLen + 1) + aroonLen) / aroonLen
aroonOsc = aroonUp - aroonDn

aroonOk = aroonMode == "off" ? true :
     aroonMode == "osc >= 0" ? aroonOsc >= 0.0 :
     aroonMode == "osc >= 50" ? aroonOsc >= 50.0 :
     aroonMode == "osc >= -50" ? aroonOsc >= -50.0 : aroonUp >= 70.0

donHi = ta.highest(high, donEntry)[1]
donLo = ta.lowest(low, donExit)[1]

gateOk = (not useAdx or adxVal >= adxMin) and (not useChop or chopVal <= chopMax)
breakout = close > donHi
atrOk = not na(atrVal) and atrVal > 0
warm = bar_index > math.max(math.max(emaSlow * 3, donEntry + 2), math.max(aroonLen + 2, 30))

signal = breakout and emaOk and gateOk and aroonOk and atrOk and warm

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ORDERS. Three rules of this branch's Pine discipline are load-bearing here:
//
//  1. `barstate.isconfirmed` guards the entry, so ticking the Strategy Tester's "Script execution"
//     boxes cannot change the report. Without it a mid-bar `close` fires signals on bars that never
//     satisfied the rule. If a checkbox changes the report, the report is about the checkbox.
//  2. THE EXIT BRACKET IS PLACED WITH THE ENTRY, as a FILL-RELATIVE `loss` in ticks, using the ATR
//     stored at the SIGNAL bar. `strategy.exit` only runs on a bar where a position already exists,
//     so writing it a bar later leaves the entry bar naked -- 4.4 to 13.0% of trades at -33 to -118
//     points when that was last measured (STUDY_PINE_PARITY / STUDY_V56).
//  3. THE EXIT BAR IS RECORDED BEFORE THE ENTRY TEST RUNS on the same bar. A stale marker lets the
//     script re-enter on the bar a trade closed -- 95 extra trades on 15m when that was last
//     measured. Position state is read through `strategy.closedtrades`, not by watching
//     `strategy.position_size[1]`, which misses a trade that opens and stops out inside ONE bar.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var float pendAtr = na
var int signalBar = na
var bool pending = false

// (3) resolve the pending order FIRST, so the entry test below sees current state. This reads
// ONLY `bar_index`, which does not vary mid-bar: a market order submitted at the close of bar b
// is resolved by the open of b+1, one way or the other.
if pending and not na(signalBar) and bar_index > signalBar
    pending := false

flat = strategy.position_size == 0 and not pending
inTrade = strategy.position_size > 0
pastFillBar = not na(signalBar) and bar_index > signalBar + 1

// the researched channel exit: close below the prior donExit-bar low, never on the fill bar.
// IT FILLS AT THE NEXT BAR'S OPEN. The engine fills at THIS bar's close, which no script can do.
channelExit = inTrade and pastFillBar and not na(donLo) and close < donLo

if channelExit and barstate.isconfirmed
    strategy.close("L", comment = "channel")

if signal and flat and barstate.isconfirmed
    pendAtr := atrVal
    signalBar := bar_index
    pending := true
    stopTicks = math.max(math.round(stopN * pendAtr / syminfo.mintick), 1)
    profTicks = tpR > 0.0 ? math.max(math.round(tpR * stopN * pendAtr / syminfo.mintick), 1) : na
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    strategy.exit("Lx", from_entry = "L", loss = stopTicks, profit = profTicks, comment = "stop/tp")

// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DIAGNOSTICS. The counters exist so the Aroon claim is testable on YOUR chart rather than on
// trust: `aroon pass on breakouts` is the whole finding, live.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var int nBreak = 0
var int nAroonOnBreak = 0
var int nEmaOnBreak = 0
var int nGateOnBreak = 0
var int nSignal = 0

if barstate.isconfirmed and warm
    if breakout and atrOk
        nBreak += 1
        if aroonOk
            nAroonOnBreak += 1
        if emaOk
            nEmaOnBreak += 1
        if gateOk
            nGateOnBreak += 1
    if signal
        nSignal += 1

pctBreak(k) => nBreak > 0 ? str.tostring(100.0 * k / nBreak, "#.0") + "%" : "--"

plot(showLevelsIn ? donHi : na, "Donchian entry", color.new(color.teal, 0), 1, plot.style_stepline)
plot(showLevelsIn ? donLo : na, "Donchian exit", color.new(color.maroon, 0), 1, plot.style_stepline)
// NOT drawn on the price scale: an overlay strategy has no second pane, and a -100..100 series on
// a price axis makes the chart unreadable. Status line and Data Window only.
plot(showAroonIn ? aroonOsc : na, "Aroon oscillator", color.new(color.orange, 0), 1,
     display = display.data_window + display.status_line)
plot(showAroonIn ? aroonUp : na, "Aroon up", color.new(color.green, 0), 1,
     display = display.data_window + display.status_line)
plotshape(signal and barstate.isconfirmed, "signal", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar,
     color.new(color.teal, 0), size = size.tiny)

if showHudIn and barstate.islast
    var table hud = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 13, border_width = 1)
    identity = aroonMode != "off" and aroonLen <= donEntry
    table.cell(hud, 0, 0, "V60", bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 70), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 0, preset, bgcolor = color.new(color.teal, 70), text_size = size.small)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 1, "EMA", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 1, emaMode == "off" ? "off" : emaMode == "state" ?
         str.tostring(emaFast) + "/" + str.tostring(emaSlow) + " state" :
         str.tostring(emaFast) + "/" + str.tostring(emaSlow) + " cross w" +
         str.tostring(confirmWin), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 2, "Donchian", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 2, str.tostring(donEntry) + " in / " + str.tostring(donExit) + " out",
         text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 3, "stop / tp", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 3, str.tostring(stopN, "#.##") + "N / " +
         (tpR > 0.0 ? str.tostring(tpR, "#.#") + "R" : "none"), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 4, "gate", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 4, (useAdx ? "ADX>=" + str.tostring(adxMin, "#.#") + " " : "") +
         (useChop ? "CHOP<=" + str.tostring(chopMax, "#.#") : "") +
         (not useAdx and not useChop ? "off" : ""), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 5, "aroon", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 5, aroonMode == "off" ? "off" : aroonMode + " (" + str.tostring(aroonLen) +
         ")", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 6, "breakout bars", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 6, str.tostring(nBreak), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 7, "aroon pass on breakouts", text_size = size.tiny,
         bgcolor = identity ? color.new(color.orange, 60) : na)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 7, pctBreak(nAroonOnBreak), text_size = size.tiny,
         bgcolor = identity ? color.new(color.orange, 60) : na)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 8, "EMA pass on breakouts", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 8, pctBreak(nEmaOnBreak), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 9, "gate pass on breakouts", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 9, pctBreak(nGateOnBreak), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 10, "signals", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 10, str.tostring(nSignal), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 11, "closed trades", text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 11, str.tostring(strategy.closedtrades), text_size = size.tiny)
    table.cell(hud, 0, 12, identity ? "AROON IS INERT HERE" : "aroon length vs channel",
         text_size = size.tiny, bgcolor = identity ? color.new(color.orange, 60) : na)
    table.cell(hud, 1, 12, identity ? "len " + str.tostring(aroonLen) + " <= entry " +
         str.tostring(donEntry) : "len " + str.tostring(aroonLen) + " vs entry " +
         str.tostring(donEntry), text_size = size.tiny,
         bgcolor = identity ? color.new(color.orange, 60) : na)
